<$fill $name="body">

!! Keys

|!Shortcut tiddler |!Default |!Action |
|`outline-up` / `outline-down` |Up / Down |Select previous / next unit. A whole list counts as one block: Down from a selected list goes to the block after it, Up from below a list selects the whole list; inside a list they go item by item |
|`outline-up-deep` / `outline-down-deep` |ctrl-Up / ctrl-Down |Select previous / next unit in document order, also into lists (from below a list: its last item) |
|`outline-parent` / `outline-child` |Left / Right |Select the parent unit (item of a sub-item, whole list of a top-level item, heading of a section) / the first child |
|`outline-move-up` / `outline-move-down` |alt-Up / alt-Down |Swap with previous / next sibling |
|`outline-indent` / `outline-promote` |Tab / shift-Tab |Demote / promote by one level |
|`outline-edit` |Enter |Edit in place (on a transclusion Enter opens the target) |
|`outline-add` |ctrl-Enter |Edit a new empty unit below the selected one (see New unit) |
|`outline-delete` |Delete |Delete the unit with its subtree, after a confirmation menu (see Delete) |
|`outline-undo` / `outline-redo` |ctrl-Z / ctrl-Y, ctrl-shift-Z |Undo / redo the last change made in the outline (see Undo) |
|`outline-menu` |alt-Enter |Block menu: insert a new block after or before the unit, or turn it into another type; Up/Down, Enter runs, Escape closes. In the editor: save, then only //Turn into//; the editor opens again on the unit, also after Escape |
|`outline-open` |Enter |Open the transclusion target in outline mode |
|`outline-clear` |Escape |Clear selection; with nothing selected: put the outline to sleep |
|`outline-save` |ctrl-Enter |Save the edit |
|`outline-continue` |Enter |Save and open a new unit (single-line units). In the middle of a list item's text: split it (see Split); at the start of a filled list item or paragraph: a new empty one above (see New unit) |
|`outline-newline` |shift-Enter |Newline in the editor (saved as `<br>` in list items and headings) |
|`outline-indent` / `outline-promote` |Tab / shift-Tab |In the editor too: save, indent / promote, keep editing. On an empty new list item: its level (see New unit) |
|`outline-move-up` / `outline-move-down` |alt-Up / alt-Down |In the editor too: save, move, keep editing |
|`outline-edit-up` |ctrl-Up |Editor only: save and edit the previous unit |
|`outline-edit-down` |ctrl-Down |Editor only: save and edit the next unit |
|`outline-merge` |Backspace |Editor, caret at the start of a list item: merge it into the item above (see Merge) |
|`outline-merge-next` |Delete |Editor, caret at the end of a list item: pull the item below up into it (see Merge) |
|`outline-cancel` |Escape |Discard the edit |
|`outline-help` |shift-slash |Show / hide the key overview. `?` always works too, whatever the keyboard layout; Escape closes it |

All are `$:/config/shortcuts/<name>`; descriptions are in `$:/config/ShortcutInfo/<name>`. Change them in the settings tab (the core shortcut editor, press the key to record it, platform variants included) or in ControlPanel > Keyboard Shortcuts.

Copy, cut and paste (Ctrl-C / Ctrl-X / Ctrl-V, Cmd on Mac) are the browser's own keys, not shortcut tiddlers (see Clipboard).

!! Type badges

|!`data-ol-type` |!Unit |
|`paragraph`, `code-block`, `table`, `quote`, `rule` |Blocks (`p`, `pre`, `table`, `blockquote`, `hr`; other blocks: their tag name) |
|`h1` … `h6` |Headings |
|`bullet`, `numbered`, `term`, `definition`, `quote` |List items (by their list: `ul`, `ol`, `dt`/`dd`, `blockquote`) |
|`bullet-list`, `numbered-list`, `definitions`, `quote` |Whole lists (badge in the left margin) |
|`transclusion`, `widget` |Transclusion lines, widgets and macro calls |
|tag name (`div`, ...) |Opened HTML containers (badge in the left margin) |

The widget sets `data-ol-type` on each unit's first DOM node (`unitType` in `dom-utils.js`); CSS shows it as `::after`, absolutely positioned, so the layout does not change. The editor field gets the type of the unit it edits, of the chosen block type, or of its anchor (a new item); an item edited inside its `li` keeps the `li`'s badge.

!! Key overview

The //keys// tab and the overlay (`?` in an outline, or the small ? button at its top right) show the same table, `$:/plugins/rimir/outline/ui/keys-table`, with the keys read live from the config. Its groups are the tiddlers listed in `$:/plugins/rimir/outline/key-groups`: each has a `caption`, an optional `hint`, a `list` of shortcut names and, optionally, text shown after the keys (the fixed block menu keys). The settings tab uses the same groups.

A double-click on a unit opens the editor on it (on a transclusion: its line; links and buttons keep their click). While another unit is edited, that one is saved first (like Ctrl-Up/Down; a refused save keeps its editor open with the notice).

In multi-line units (code blocks, tables, widgets, `"""` items) Enter is a plain newline and only Ctrl-Enter saves.

!! Indent and promote

* Lists: a list item and its subtree lines get one more of the item's last marker character (`#b` becomes `##b`, `*b` `**b`, `#*` `#**`). No previous sibling: no-op. Promote removes one marker character; depth 1 is a no-op.
* Headings: one `!` more on the heading and every heading in its section; no-op if one would pass 6. Promote removes one; level 1 is a no-op.
* Other units: Tab and Shift-Tab do nothing.

!! Move

Swap the unit's whole subtree with the adjacent sibling's whole subtree, blank-line separators preserved. Blocks other than items and headings that touch (a single line break) get a blank line between them and before the following content, so a paragraph cannot absorb its neighbour. First/last child: no-op.

* List item: siblings are items of the same list at the same depth.
* Heading: siblings are headings of the same level in the same parent.
* Other blocks: siblings are blocks in the same section (or HTML container, or root) before any sub-heading.

Across heading lines (blocks of a section, never out of an HTML container):

* A heading moves up over the block or deeper heading above it: its line goes above that block, which joins its section (`para`, `! New` → `! New`, `para`).
* A heading moves down over a following higher heading: its section goes below that heading's line and becomes a sub-section (`!! B`, `y`, `! A` → `! A`, `!! B`, `y`).
* A block (paragraph, list, ...) at the end of a section moves down over the next heading line into that section; as the first block of a section it moves up over the heading line out of it. The two are each other's inverse.

A heading moving down over a heading of the same level swaps the two sections, as before; one with blocks under it does not move down over them (use Alt-Up on the block, or on the next heading).

!! Delete

The unit goes with its subtree: an item with its sub-items, a heading with its section, a list with its items, a container with its contents. An only item takes its list along and an only child its container (neither can stay empty). Separators as for a blank save: one blank line stays between the neighbours. The selection goes to the unit that now starts there.

|!Selected |!Menu |
|Heading with a section |Yes, the heading and its section (N blocks) · Just the heading (its section joins the one above) · Cancel |
|Whole list / item with sub-items / container |Yes, ... (N items / sub-items / blocks) · Cancel |
|Anything else |Yes, delete · Cancel |

The first entry is active: Delete, Enter deletes; Escape cancels. List items without sub-items are deleted at once while `$:/config/rimir/outline/quick-delete-items` is `yes` (the default); `no` asks for them too. The model guard refuses a result that removes other units than these (e.g. two lists that would merge).

!! Undo

In selection mode Ctrl-Z takes back the last change made in the outline: a move, indent, delete, merge, split, conversion or saved edit; Ctrl-Y (or Ctrl-Shift-Z) does it again. The selection goes back to where it was before the change. A split or merge, and Tab / Alt-Up/Down while editing, save the edited text and change the structure in one step. Inside the editor Ctrl-Z and Ctrl-Y are the outline's undo and redo while the field still has the text it opened with (nothing typed, or the typing undone): so a split, merge or move made from the editor is taken back at once, and the editor opens again on the unit selected afterwards. With typed text they are the text field's own.

The history is kept per tiddler in `$:/temp/rimir/outline/undo/<title>` for the running session only, the last `$:/config/rimir/outline/undo-depth` steps (default 20). A new change empties the redo steps. Undo writes only while the tiddler still has the text the outline left: when it was changed elsewhere (another editor, a sync), the history is dropped and nothing is written. Read-only wikis: nothing.

!! Clipboard

In selection mode Ctrl-C copies the selected unit with its subtree (an item with its sub-items, a heading with its section, a whole list, a container with its contents) to the system clipboard, Ctrl-X cuts it: the same, then it is deleted without the Delete menu (Ctrl-Z brings it back). Ctrl-V pastes after the selected unit and selects what it pasted; in a tiddler without units it goes at the end. These are the browser's own copy, cut and paste (Cmd on Mac, the Edit menu works too), so the keys cannot be changed in the shortcut settings. A copied unit flashes briefly. In the editor, and while text is marked with the mouse, they act on text as usual; read-only wikis: copy only.

A copy puts three formats on the clipboard:

|!Format |!Content |!Used by |
|`text/html` |the unit rendered (its wikitext source rendered in this tiddler's context), without CSS classes; links to tiddlers become their text |e-mail, Jira and other rich text editors |
|`text/plain` |the wikitext source |text fields, a TiddlyWiki editor |
|`application/x-rimir-outline` |JSON `{kind, source}` (kind `items`, `heading` or `block`) |a paste into an outline, also in another tab or wiki |

In the HTML and the plain text, copied list items start at level 1 (a sub-item copied alone has no empty bullets above it); the outline format keeps the source as it is. A paste takes the outline format when it is there, else the plain text as wikitext: one list is pasted as items, one heading with its section as a heading, anything else as it is. HTML from elsewhere is not converted, only its plain text is used.

The levels adapt to the place (only real list markers and heading `!`s change, not lines inside a code block):

|!Copied \ selected |!List item |!Whole list |!Heading |!Other block |
|Items |after the item's sub-items, at its level; sub-items keep their extra marker characters (`* a`, `** a1` after `## y` → `## a`, `##* a1`) |at the end of the list, at its top level |a new list right below the heading line |a new list after the block |
|Heading |after the outermost list |after the list |after the heading's section, at its level |after the block |
|Block |after the outermost list |after the list |right below the heading line |after the block |

A new list starts at level 1 (`#* a`, `#** b` → `* a`, `** b`). A heading after anything but a heading gets one level below the heading of the section it lands in (level 1 outside any section); its sub-headings keep their distance, at most level 6. Blocks are set apart by blank lines.

!! Merge (Backspace)

In the editor, caret at the very start of a list item (nothing selected): the item's text goes to the end of the item above it in the list (the previous item in document order: the parent, or the last sub-item of the previous sibling), the item's line goes, its sub-items keep their lines and levels. The editor continues in the item above, at the join. An empty item is simply deleted (also one with sub-items) and the editor goes to the end of the item above; an empty new item is discarded the same way. The first item of a list, other units and multi-line items: a normal Backspace.

Delete with the caret at the very end of a list item is the same merge from above: the item below that Backspace would merge into this one (the next item in document order: the first sub-item, or the next item of the list) comes up, the caret stays at the join. The last item of a list, blank, new and multi-line items: a normal Delete.

!! Split (Enter)

In the editor, caret inside a list item's text (not at its start or end, nothing selected): the text before the caret stays in the item, the text after it goes to a new item directly below, which is edited with the caret at its start. The new item is a sibling with the same marker; when the item has sub-items it becomes their first one, so the sub-items stay with the item. Backspace at the new item's start (merge) gives back the original line.

!! Empty tiddler

A tiddler without units (empty, or only whitespace and comments) shows a hint. Enter (or Ctrl-Enter) opens the editor for a first paragraph, Alt-Enter the block menu with the insert types only; the block goes at the end of the text.

!! New unit (Enter)

Enter at the end of the editor saves and opens a new unit after the edited one; Ctrl-Enter in selection mode opens the same new unit after the selected one, without editing that first:

* List item (also a quote line): same marker, after the item's whole subtree. While it is still empty, Tab / Shift-Tab set its level (one marker character more / less; at most one level below the item above it, at least level 1); the field moves with it and it is written with that marker.
* Heading: paragraph directly under the heading line.
* Paragraph, and anything else (code block, table, whole list, ...): paragraph after it.

Enter with the caret at the very start of a filled list item or paragraph saves the edited text and opens an empty new unit right above it: an item with the same marker (sub-items stay with the item below), or a paragraph. Escape or an empty save leaves the text as it was.

!! Block menu

Insert before offers the same types as Insert after and puts the block directly above the selected unit (it ends the section above; above a list or a lower heading this is the way to put a heading in front of it). Turning a heading into another level (Heading 1 to 3) changes only its own `!`s: its class and text stay, the headings of its section keep their levels (Tab / Shift-Tab change the whole section, also to levels 4 to 6). Turning a paragraph or heading into a bulleted or numbered item next to a list of that type joins that list (TW continues a list over blank lines).

Turn into: everything turns into everything, with one rule: a multi-line unit (paragraph, code block, quote block, typed block) turns into a one-line type (heading, list item, quote line) only while its content is one line. A list item with `<br>`s is one line; turned into a block its `<br>`s become line breaks. The `turn-into` field of a type narrows the list.

|!Selected |!Insert after / before |!Turn into |
|Paragraph, code block, quote block, typed block |every type with the `block` context |every other type (one-line types only for one-line content) |
|Heading |the same (a heading goes after the section, other blocks right below the heading) |every other type; its section joins the section above |
|Top-level list item |item types: a sibling with the item's marker (Insert before on the first item: a new first bullet); other types: before / after the whole list. Plus //Add to this item// |every other type: as a block it leaves its list (the list splits, its sub-items stay a list below it, one level up) |
|Sub-item |the same |the other item types (with all its siblings of that level) |
|Whole list |the same |the other item types (all levels) |
|Transclusion |the same, plus //Edit this line// first (a diagram: //Edit <title>//) |– |

!! Block types

The block menu, Turn into and the badges of new blocks follow the tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/rimir/outline/BlockType`, in tag order (the tag tiddler's `list`, `list-before` / `list-after` on a type). Outline ships its types as shadows under `$:/plugins/rimir/outline/blocktypes/`; override one to rename it (`caption`), or remove its tag to hide it. A tiddler with missing fields is skipped.

|!Field |!Meaning |
|`name` |Key, unique |
|`caption` |Menu label |
|`badge` |Badge of a new block's editor field and of typed blocks of the type |
|`behaviour` |`paragraph`, `heading` (`level` 1–6), `item` (`marker` `*`, `#` or `>`), `fenced` (`open`, `close` lines), `typed` (`content-type`: a `$$$<content-type>` … `$$$` block) |
|`starter` |Text a new block or diagram starts with |
|`contexts` |`block` (insert before / after blocks) and / or `item` (//Add to this item//); default `block` |
|`inline` |For the `item` context: `transclude` (a new tiddler of `content-type`, transcluded) or a template with `$content$`, e.g. `<<pill "$content$">>` |
|`turn-into` |Filter over type names: the types a unit of this type may turn into |

Overriding a built-in type's `badge` changes only its new-block editor field; units on the page keep their badge from the rendered element.

!! Add to this item and diagram editing

On a list item, //Add to this item// lists the types with the `item` context. A `transclude` type opens a code field below the item with the type's starter text; nothing is written until Ctrl-Enter, which creates the tiddler `<item text> (<badge>)` (plain text, at most about 40 characters; the host title for an item without text; made unique) of the type's content type and appends `{{title}}` to the item's line (Ctrl-Z removes the reference, the tiddler stays). A template type appends the filled template. Escape writes nothing. A transcluded diagram (inline in a unit, or a block-level transclusion line) opens the same field on its tiddler's text: double-click, Enter on the line, or //Edit <title>// in the block menu; Ctrl-Enter saves into that tiddler, Escape discards. The field has the orange frame of another tiddler's content; only Ctrl-Enter and Escape are outline keys in it.

!! State and config

|!Tiddler |!Purpose |
|`$:/temp/rimir/outline/...` |Editor buffer, selection, open key overview (`help/<title>`), undo history (`undo/<title>`, JSON) while active. While a tiddler's selection or buffer exists its outline is awake; closing the tiddler deletes them |
|`$:/config/rimir/outline/enabled` |`yes` (default): every eligible tiddler has the outline, woken with Ctrl-Click; `no`: none |
|Field `outline: no` |Leaves this tiddler out |
|`$:/config/rimir/outline/badges` |Type badges: `all` (default), `headings` (h1–h6 only) or `off`. Sets class `rr-ol-badges-<mode>` on the frame; the badge text is the unit's `data-ol-type` |
|`$:/config/rimir/outline/quick-delete-items` |`yes` (default): Delete removes list items without sub-items without asking; `no`: always ask |
|`$:/config/rimir/outline/undo-depth` |Number of undo steps kept per tiddler (default 20) |
|`$:/config/rimir/outline/full-editor` |`yes`: full text editor with toolbar; otherwise (default `no`) the compact one-line editor |

</$fill>
